## Key Findings

- The dataset originally contained 2,225 articles.
- No missing or empty article texts were detected.
- Removing 98 duplicate records reduced the dataset to 2,127 articles.
- The five classes contain different numbers of articles.
- Common English words appeared frequently in the vocabulary.
- Some articles contained URLs, digits, special characters, or potential encoding issues.
- Text normalization provided a consistent starting point for machine learning experiments.

## Next Steps

The normalized dataset will be used to train a news classification model using **TF-IDF and Logistic Regression**.

Additional preprocessing techniques, including stopword removal and lemmatization, can be compared against the normalized-text baseline to evaluate their impact on classification performance.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the importance of Exploratory Data Analysis and text preprocessing before training machine learning models.

The analysis helped identify data quality issues, understand text characteristics, and prepare a normalized dataset for future classification experiments.
